{"id":328,"name":"trapinch","speciesId":328,"dex":328,"form":"normal","generation":3,"types":["ground"],"stats":{"hp":45,"attack":100,"defense":45,"special-attack":45,"special-defense":45,"speed":10},"abilities":[{"name":"hyper-cutter","hidden":false},{"name":"arena-trap","hidden":false},{"name":"sheer-force","hidden":true}],"height":7,"weight":150,"baseExp":58,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/328.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/328.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/328.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/328.ogg","genus":"Ant Pit Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"ruby","text":"TRAPINCH’s nest is a sloped, bowl-like pit dug in sand. This POKéMON patiently waits for prey to tumble down the pit. Its giant jaws have enough strength to crush even boulders."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"TRAPINCH is a patient hunter. It digs an inescapable pit in a desert and waits for its prey to come tumbling down. This POKéMON can go a whole week without access to any water."},{"version":"emerald","text":"Its big jaws crunch through boulders. Because its head is so big, it has a hard time getting back upright if it tips over onto its back."},{"version":"firered","text":"It lives in arid deserts. It makes a sloping pit trap in sand where it patiently awaits prey."},{"version":"diamond","text":"It makes a conical pit in desert sand and lies in wait at the bottom for prey to come tumbling down."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"Its nest is a sloped, bowl-like pit in the desert. Once something has fallen in, there is no escape."},{"version":"black-2","text":"It makes an inescapable conical pit and lies in wait at the bottom for prey to come tumbling down."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Trapinch’s nest is a sloped, bowl-lik